sophia: Anyone seen this in middleware? Importing the SDK in Next edge middleware throws: `ReferenceError: require is not defined`. deployed on Vercel edge.
leo: yep, saw it earlier when we upgraded SDK -> 2.x. Looks like bundler picks CJS entry or a transitive package uses require.
sophia: repro: middleware.ts -> `import { createClient } from '@redwood-inference/sdk'` then runtime crash. local dev bundling ok, only on edge.
rita: middleware/edge is strict ESM + no node builtins. If package.json exports don't guide bundlers, Next might resolve the `main` cjs file. SDK needs an explicit edge/browser export or a pure ESM build.
leo: sample package.json exports suggestion: 
```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/index.cjs",
    "edge": "./dist/index.edge.mjs",
    "browser": "./dist/index.browser.mjs"
  }
}
```
rita: + add a `types` entry that points to `dist/index.d.ts` and ship a `dist/index.edge.d.ts` for edge typings. TS complains if you alias to a tiny wrapper without types.
sophia: short-term workaround that worked for me: add a webpack alias in next.config.js to a tiny edge-only proxy.
```js
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  webpack(config) {
    config.resolve.alias['@redwood-inference/sdk'] = require.resolve('./src/edge-sdk-proxy.js');
    return config;
  }
};
```
rita: what did edge-sdk-proxy.js look like?
sophia: minimal fetch wrapper, no node deps: 
```js
// src/edge-sdk-proxy.js
export async function embed(req) {
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/embeddings', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { "Authorization": `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}` },
    body: JSON.stringify(req)
  });
  return r.json();
}
export default { embed };
```
leo: for TS add `src/edge-sdk-proxy.d.ts` with `export function embed(body: any): Promise<any>;` so middleware typing is happy.
rita: longer term asks for SDK team: 1) publish an official `edge` export and `browser` build 2) strip Node-only shims behind conditional exports (debug/logger) 3) run an edge smoke test in CI that simulates Next edge resolution.
dev-bot: CI update: added next-edge-smoke job to matrix. failing on sdk@2.1.7 due to `require('debug')` in logger shim — see https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/issues/427
sophia: opened an internal doc (link: https://redwood.company/devex/edge-middleware-recipe) with the alias & proxy snippet + ts fix. Posting this to teams who run middleware (payments, webhooks).
leo: small note: dynamic import (`await import('@redwood-inference/sdk')`) didn't help for me — resolver still pulled CJS.
sophia: ok will add the alias recipe in the repo and follow up when SDK issue is fixed. thanks all :raised_hands:
